        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-cpe" data-main="vulns" data-sub="cpe">
            <h3>CPE mapping (installed program name &rarr; CVE codes)</h3>
            <div class="info">
                Every NVD CVE names the affected software with a technical code, a <strong>CPE</strong> like
                <code>cpe:...:mozilla:firefox</code>. This table is the dictionary that tells the scanner which
                code belongs to which program on your PCs:
                <ul style="margin:6px 0 6px 18px;padding:0;">
                    <li><strong>Regex</strong> is matched case-insensitively against the installed program name.</li>
                    <li><strong>Vendor / Product</strong> is the CPE code that gets searched in the CVE database.</li>
                    <li><strong>License type</strong> is how that product is licensed - an SPDX identifier
                    (<code>MIT</code>, <code>GPL-2.0-only</code>, &hellip;) or one of <code>Proprietary</code>
                    (a license has to be bought), <code>Freeware</code> (closed source, free of charge) or
                    <code>Freeware (non-commercial)</code>. It is curated once in the table, so the software CSV,
                    the software list and the asset push report it without re-deriving anything per device - and
                    an empty cell honestly means "no verified statement about this product". What a
                    <em>specific</em> machine holds (Retail / OEM / Volume, activated or not) is measured on that
                    device instead: see Software &rsaquo; License keys.</li>
                </ul>
                Rows labelled <em>Remote</em> come from the maintained table file <code>cpe-table.json</code>
                (shipped with the plugin, refreshed from its repository URL); rows labelled <em>Custom</em> are
                your own additions and are always checked first, so they win over any remote row. Programs that
                match no row here are still checked automatically against the product names present in the NVD
                data (the <em>Auto-map</em> switch under Settings). Only software where even that proves nothing
                is listed as <em>not assessable</em> - never as "clean".
                <br><br>
                <strong>Fix a wrong row:</strong> <em>Override</em> copies it as a custom entry you can edit,
                <em>Delete</em> removes only your custom entries, never remote ones.
            </div>
            <div class="setgrid">
                <label for="setCpeTableEnabled">Update mapping table from repository</label>
                <div><input type="checkbox" id="setCpeTableEnabled">
                    <div class="hint">The curated table is maintained as <code>cpe-table.json</code> in this plugin's GitHub repository,
                    shipped inside the plugin and re-downloaded with every NVD feed refresh. Off (or unreachable): only your custom
                    entries below and the automatic matching remain.</div></div>
                <label for="setCpeTableUrl">Mapping table URL</label>
                <div><input type="text" id="setCpeTableUrl" style="width:420px">
                    <select id="setCpeTableUrlSrc" class="srcsel"></select>
                    <div class="hint">https only. Only change this if you maintain your own table copy.</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="hint" id="cpeTableSourceInfo"></div>
            <div class="filter-row">
                <input type="text" id="cpeFilter" class="filter-input" placeholder="Filter mappings by regex, vendor or product...">
            </div>
            <div class="table-container">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th style="cursor:default">Regex (display name)</th>
                            <th style="cursor:default">Vendor</th>
                            <th style="cursor:default">Product</th>
                            <th style="cursor:default">License type</th>
                            <th style="cursor:default">Source</th>
                            <th style="cursor:default"></th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody id="cpeTableBody"></tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <h4 style="font-size:13px;color:#0b3d6b;margin:14px 0 6px 0;">Add / Override mapping</h4>
            <div class="controls">
                <input id="cpeRegex" type="text" placeholder="Regex, e.g. ^SAS Studio" style="min-width:220px;">
                <input id="cpeVendor" type="text" placeholder="CPE vendor, e.g. mozilla" style="min-width:160px;">
                <input id="cpeProduct" type="text" placeholder="CPE product, e.g. firefox" style="min-width:160px;">
                <input id="cpeLicenseType" type="text" placeholder="License type, e.g. MPL-2.0 / Proprietary / Freeware (optional)" style="min-width:220px;">
                <button id="addCpeBtn" data-help="cpe.add">Add</button>
            </div>
            <div id="cpeMsg"></div>
            <div class="controls" style="margin-top:16px;"><button id="saveSettingsBtn2" data-help="set.save">Save CPE settings</button></div>
            <div id="vulnDataMsg"></div>
        </div>
